<article class="env-lemma" id="0DM8">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0DM8">Lemma <span data-tag="0DM8">108.7.3</span>.</a> Assume $X \to B$ is proper as well as of finite presentation. Then $\mathrm{Hilb}_{X/B} \to B$ satisfies the existence part of the valuative criterion (Morphisms of Spaces, Definition <a href="/tag/03IX" data-tag="03IX">67.41.1</a>). </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      In Quot, Lemma <a href="/tag/0D00" data-tag="0D00">99.9.2</a> we have seen that $\mathrm{Hilb}_{X/B} = \mathrm{Quot}_{\mathcal{O}_ X/X/B}$. Hence this follows from Lemma <a href="/tag/0DM4" data-tag="0DM4">108.5.3</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>